  "contract": [
    "Read the complete finite control BYTE sequence through its first NUL before any source payload, including when source is empty. Set bits only for nonzero bytes; duplicates retain their own reads and writes.",
    "Then read one volatile unsigned BYTE per reached source position. Explicit source NUL stops before membership/its own advance and returns null. Every nonzero source byte saves genuine current, advances actual cursor, then checks membership; first hit returns saved current without reread or pointer subtraction.",
    "Empty control still scans source. Source needs only the reached finite prefix through first NUL or first nonzero control member; an early member needs no later terminator or full unused extent.",
    "Reached inputs are genuine live stable determinate readable raw bytes, with nonwrapping32bit advances within/onepast their own actual allocations, including terminal nonzero source advance; never dereference onepast. No padding or wider input-object requirement.",
    "Admit raw unaligned/interior/prefix/read-only/identical/overlapping inputs and ordinary stable caller-owned stack storage. The result is a genuine borrowed source pointer with no ownership, lifetime or access-permission transfer.",
    "Exclude faults, mutation/concurrency, MMIO/volatile protocols, lifetime changes and native callee frame/home/saved-register/private-bitmap self-alias protocols. No fake native scratch identity or Source parameter.",
    "No null guard, runtime validation, signed cap, Unicode/locale/codepage/case meaning, SDK search/copy/memcpy/strpbrk, provider, fallback, global/TLS, caller binding or call to new strcspn."
  ],
